  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame and `vite build` hasn't run. The scene has seven crystals built with `geometry.define`. Each is a 5–7-sided prism with a narrowed top and a pointed tip. Heights and tilts differ. Every side quad and tip triangle gets its own vertex colour (cyan, violet and magenta hues) with flat per-face normals. The crystals are merged into one mesh that spins slowly around Y on a dark cylinder pedestal. The background is near-black with fog, bloom and a dim cool key light. Cyan, magenta and violet point lights sit behind and beside the cluster as rim lights. An additive particle emitter (`effects.particles`) over the pedestal disc should release glittering sparks that drift up. I set `window.__EVAL_READY__` on the second frame callback.\n\nTwo things to check when it's run:\n- **Sparks:** the typed API takes `gravity` and `noise` as plain numbers, so I used `gravity: -0.25` to lift the sparks. I haven't confirmed they rise rather than sink.\n- **Rotation units:** I assumed `setRotation` takes radians, based on the docs example.",
